\f0\fs48 \cf2 MLB Analytics App by Chris Jones v1.1\

\fs24 \cf0 \
\
A command\uc0\u8209 line application for running MLB team analytics, standings projections, free agent evaluations, and R\'b2 analysis with visualizations based on data from 2015-present day.\
\
\cf3 _____________________________________________________________________________________\
\cf0 \
\uc0\u55357 \u56514  Folder Contents\
- `mlb_analytics_app.py` \uc0\u8594  The launcher script (menu interface).\
- `standings_projections.py` \uc0\u8594  Runs full standings projections based on WAR and finance data.\
- `single_team_simulator.py` \uc0\u8594  Evaluates a single team\'92s projected performance via WAR.\
- `free_agent_evaluator.py` \uc0\u8594  Adds a free agent to team projections.\
- `r2_analysis.py` \uc0\u8594  Runs R\'b2 analysis with visualizations.\
- `projected_mlb_team_data.csv` \uc0\u8594  Projected WAR data for all teams.\
- `mlb_finance_data_1.csv` \uc0\u8594  Historical finance/performance dataset.\
- `2026_freeagents.csv` \uc0\u8594  Free agent list for 2026.\
- Output files (e.g. `jonesy_mlb_projected_standings.csv`) will be generated here.\
